; Find a record by id in a table of records that start with an id
;
; Steps through records of 3 bytes from IX until the first byte equals A or is
; $FF (the end mark). Used on #R$C063 (objects), the picture table, the verb
; tables and others. HL, DE and BC are kept (the alternate set is used).
;
; A Id looked for
; IX Start of the table
; O:IX Address of the matching record, or of the end mark
; O:F Z set when the id was not found (end mark reached)
@label=FindIdRecord
c$9DBD EXX
 $9DBE PUSH IX
 $9DC0 POP HL
 $9DC1 LD B,A
@isub=LD E,ID_ENTRY_SIZE
 $9DC2 LD E,$03
 $9DC4 LD D,$00
*$9DC6 LD A,(HL)
 $9DC7 CP B
 $9DC8 JR Z,$9DD2
@isub=CP END_MARK
 $9DCA CP $FF
 $9DCC JR Z,$9DD2
 $9DCE ADD HL,DE
 $9DCF JP $9DC6
*$9DD2 PUSH HL
 $9DD3 POP IX
@isub=CP END_MARK
 $9DD5 CP $FF           ; Z: not found
 $9DD7 EXX
 $9DD8 RET
